# Needle-X governance baseline.
# Hard limits block regressions.
# Target limits are pressure-only and should ratchet down over time.

# v0.1.34 network-aware delivery recalibration. The renderer surface admitted in
# v0.1.33 could not actually deliver captured application data: the retrieval
# substrate had 150 lines of headroom, which would have forced removing capture
# diagnostics instead of closing real gaps. The total ceiling moves once, and
# file-size discipline tightens at the same time so the new volume cannot turn
# into bigger files or new hotspots.
# 2026-10-27 strategic recalibration: measured 34,995 runtime lines after MCP
# Chromium ownership, isolated contexts and PAL process/interruptible-input
# cleanup. This adds 605 lines to the consolidated 34,390 baseline, without
# packages/dependencies. Admit that substrate, retain the LOC target and zero
# structural-issue gate, and tighten the >300-line-file ceiling from 29 to 27
# (26 observed) to offset total volume with stricter concentration control.
# 2026-10-28: admit the local typed decision observer, token-budget validation
# and advisory diagnostics (about 300 runtime lines, no new package or runtime
# dependency). Deterministic fixes remove language/payload heuristics. Keep the
# 34,500 target and every concentration/structure ceiling unchanged.
# 2026-10-29: measured 35,537 runtime lines for whole-passage claim selection,
# isolated advisory failure state, bounded MCP memo lifetime and compact scope
# diagnostics, after retiring CSS-word pruning and its genome/request profiles.
# Admit 100 lines above the former ceiling; retain the total target and tighten
# the >350-line-file ceiling from 23 to 21, target 20 (20 observed). No package/dependency
# increase. This admits a new capability, not a claimed net LOC reduction.
# 2026-10-29 acquisition policy: measured 35,983 runtime lines, service 6,768.
# Reuse the same choice adapter, dense selector, memo and trace audit owner;
# add no package/dependency or active routing engine. Admit the explicit passive
# acquisition contract and strict-render fix. Tighten >300-line files 27 -> 26
# and average file ceiling 210 -> 200 (174 observed); retain the LOC target.
# Raw HTTP download adds one streaming path shared by CLI/MCP, including
# bounded linked-asset discovery and private, rollback-capable PAL storage.
# The previous baseline uses 35,986 LOC, leaving 14 lines. The candidate
# measures 36,566 LOC, with no new package or dependency. Keep target pressure
# and cap files over 500 LOC at the six already observed.
# 2026-11-13 public-network policy and compact evidence: measured 37,469 runtime
# lines for the optional public-only egress policy (HTTP acquisition, download
# assets, redirects and the runtime-owned loopback browser filtering proxy),
# compact-by-default MCP payloads with include_diagnostics opt-in, evidence
# coverage signalling and the network_denied failure class. No new package and
# the same five runtime dependencies (12 internal packages, service 6,778).
# Admit 899 lines over the 36,570 ceiling: hard LOC 37,520, files over 300
# 26 -> 28 (27 observed); retain >350 at 21 and >500 at 6. Compensate by
# tightening the average-file hard/target ceiling 200 -> 190 (174 observed) and
# keep the 34,500 LOC target.
# 2026-11-14 fetch receipt contract: measured 37,529 runtime lines for the
# versioned fetch receipt (schema id, per-file SHA-256, stable error codes and
# adapter documentation) shared by CLI and MCP. The previous 37,520 ceiling
# left 9 lines; this admits 60 measured lines with 71 lines of headroom. No
# new package, dependency or >300-line file; retain the target, concentration
# and average-file ceilings.
# 2026-11-15 authenticated navigation session: measured 38,589 runtime lines for
# caller-provided header/cookie/Basic-auth/proxy/TLS sessions shared by
# read/query/crawl/fetch, exact-origin scoping with cross-origin redirect
# stripping, browser cookie injection, MCP/CLI surfaces, secret indirection and
# end-to-end authentication tests. The previous 37,600 ceiling left 11 lines;
# this admits 1,060 measured lines with 111 lines of headroom. No new package or
# runtime dependency. The new surface is concentrated in one platform owner and
# one transport adapter; admit the one extra >350-line file (22 observed) while
# retaining the 34,500 target, average-file and package ceilings.
# 2026-11-15 authenticated browser navigation completion: measured 39,339
# runtime lines for Chromium profile cookie import, guided browser login,
# CDP per-origin header interception, session-scoped browser proxy/insecure
# TLS launch, and linked image/font/media asset delivery. The previous 38,700
# ceiling left 111 lines; this admits 750 measured lines with 161 lines of
# headroom. No new package or runtime dependency; the service owner stays at
# 6,780 lines and the 34,500 target remains pressure. Admit three more files
# over 300 lines (31 observed) while retaining the >350, >500, package and
# average-file ceilings. Browser custom CA/client certificates and non-cookie
# profile storage remain explicit residual limits, not hidden fallbacks.
# 2026-11-15 v0.1.51 authenticated-navigation corrections: measured 39,435
# runtime lines after fixing Chromium SameSite=-1 mapping, explicit-cookie
# precedence, empty-profile handling, one-time profile validation, failed
# browser-launch reporting, all-domain browser cookie injection, browser proxy
# credential rejection, and schema/tool-catalog consistency. The 39,500 ceiling
# retains 65 lines of headroom; no new package, dependency or >300-line file.
HARD_MAX_PROD_LOC=39500
TARGET_MAX_PROD_LOC=34500

HARD_MAX_INTERNAL_PACKAGES=14
TARGET_MAX_INTERNAL_PACKAGES=11

# Direct imports are classified truthfully after go mod tidy. The five runtime
# dependencies cover HTTP, HTML, SQLite memory, YAML standards, and maintained
# WebSocket/CDP transport; none has a surface-equivalent standard-library path.
HARD_MAX_RUNTIME_DEPS=5
TARGET_MAX_RUNTIME_DEPS=4

HARD_MAX_FILE_LOC=1800
TARGET_MAX_FILE_LOC=1400

HARD_MAX_AVG_FILE_LOC=190
TARGET_MAX_AVG_FILE_LOC=190

HARD_MAX_FILES_OVER_300=31
TARGET_MAX_FILES_OVER_300=26

HARD_MAX_FILES_OVER_350=22
TARGET_MAX_FILES_OVER_350=20

HARD_MAX_FILES_OVER_500=6

HARD_MAX_PACKAGE_LOC=6800
TARGET_MAX_PACKAGE_LOC=6500

HARD_MAX_STRUCTURE_ISSUES=0
TARGET_MAX_STRUCTURE_ISSUES=0

REQUIRE_GOFUMPT=1
REQUIRE_GOVET=1
REQUIRE_STATICCHECK=1
REQUIRE_STRUCTURE_LINT=1
REQUIRE_ADVISORY_LINT=1
REQUIRE_BENCHMARK_ADVISORY_LINT=1
